cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "C(12,6,4) = 41 — computational artifact"
message: >-
  If you use this artifact, please cite both the accompanying paper and this
  software record.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Krug
    given-names: Charlie
    email: charlie@charliekrug.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-6144-9421"
abstract: >-
  Complete computational record of the determination of the covering number
  C(12,6,4) = 41. The upper bound is an explicit 41-block design checked by two
  independent programs; the lower bound is a symmetry-reduced case analysis over
  the link of a point, comprising 81 SAT instances (47 case-tree frontier nodes,
  14 exhaustiveness instances, 20 link-extension refutations), every one of which
  is refuted by a proof object replayed with drat-trim and machine-checked by
  cake_lpr, a checker extracted from a HOL4 correctness proof. All instances
  regenerate byte-for-byte from the deposited source, and every proof object is
  identified by SHA-256 in the manifests.
keywords:
  - covering design
  - covering number
  - combinatorial optimisation
  - SAT solving
  - proof certificate
  - LRAT
  - cake_lpr
  - computer-assisted proof
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-25"
references:
  - type: software
    title: cake_lpr
    abstract: >-
      Verified LRAT proof checker, extracted by CakeML from a correctness proof
      in HOL4. The verified link in this artifact's proof chain.
    authors:
      - family-names: Tan
        given-names: Yong Kiam
      - family-names: Heule
        given-names: Marijn J. H.
      - family-names: Myreen
        given-names: Magnus O.
  - type: software
